            <ArticleTitle>Can cystinosis cause coronary artery dilatation?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In children, dilated coronary arteries are usually caused by Kawasaki's disease. We report four children with dilated coronary arteries and nephropathic cystinosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
